{"agent":"fleet-capskew","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":4,"detail":"The helper appends the `ddflow.capabilities` event first and only afterwards calls `_stamp(...)`, so the stamp event lands after the capability event in the same shard. The added comment says the release \"has stamped the log first (`_stamp_and_guard`)\", but the code does the opposite. If the skew guard is order-sensitive (e.g. it only honours a capability from a version whose stamp event precedes it), then `_record` produces a log where the capability is never seen as stamped; tests such as `test_a_writer_lacking_a_recorded_capability_is_refused_just_its_kinds` would then not raise `SkewRefused` and fail. The `_stamp` call needs to be moved before the `fh.write(ev.to_json())` line to match the production sequence the helper claims to model.","digest":"65c6a8a68e5401ac","location":"tests/test_compat_capabilities.py:_record","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_compat_capabilities.py:_record"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":12819,"diff_sha":"14fc9277a28ed827c41c91c05009a1b1f7c299658a7ce12eecbffe78bcff632b","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":826.1,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"6208e9afffc24294","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B27842cfecd.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261015T190858Z-164adfc3.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewed_head":"c4fa09bcccfd33714fb8debcd8f603cfbc2ec7cc","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["tests/test_compat_capabilities.py:_record"],"tree_sha":"25629f57c5d3+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"1 finding(